WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.490
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:09.199
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.499 --> 00:00:15.379
Unit thirty-seven: Whose and Possessive 's. Today you will ask and say who owns things.

4
00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:18.343
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.637
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:24.287
Whose.

7
00:00:25.283 --> 00:00:27.724
Whose means used to ask who owns something.

8
00:00:28.317 --> 00:00:29.701
Whose bag is this?

9
00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:33.155
Your turn. Say: Whose.

10
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.048
Whose.

11
00:00:37.783 --> 00:00:38.912
Possessive 's.

12
00:00:39.917 --> 00:00:43.112
Possessive 's means the ending that shows who owns something.

13
00:00:43.717 --> 00:00:45.171
Tom's book is red.

14
00:00:45.783 --> 00:00:48.830
Your turn. Say: Possessive 's.

15
00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:52.946
Possessive 's.

16
00:00:53.683 --> 00:00:54.789
Tom's book.

17
00:00:55.783 --> 00:00:58.433
Tom's book means the book that belongs to Tom.

18
00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:00.726
Tom's book is on the desk.

19
00:01:01.317 --> 00:01:03.934
Your turn. Say: Tom's book.

20
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:07.894
Tom's book.

21
00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:09.860
The girl's bag.

22
00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:14.011
The girl's bag means the bag that belongs to the girl.

23
00:01:14.617 --> 00:01:16.175
The girl's bag is blue.

24
00:01:16.783 --> 00:01:19.947
Your turn. Say: The girl's bag.

25
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.080
The girl's bag.

26
00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:25.690
Mine.

27
00:01:26.683 --> 00:01:28.277
Mine means belonging to me.

28
00:01:28.883 --> 00:01:30.210
That pen is mine.

29
00:01:30.817 --> 00:01:33.016
Your turn. Say: Mine.

30
00:01:35.867 --> 00:01:36.670
Mine.

31
00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:38.336
Yours.

32
00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:41.001
Yours means belonging to you.

33
00:01:41.617 --> 00:01:42.920
Is this book yours?

34
00:01:43.517 --> 00:01:46.192
Your turn. Say: Yours.

35
00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:50.151
Yours.

36
00:01:50.917 --> 00:01:51.720
Owner.

37
00:01:52.717 --> 00:01:54.879
Owner means the person who has something.

38
00:01:55.483 --> 00:01:57.146
Who is the owner of this bag?

39
00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.880
Your turn. Say: Owner.

40
00:02:02.733 --> 00:02:03.444
Owner.

41
00:02:04.183 --> 00:02:05.266
Belongs to.

42
00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.215
Belongs to means is owned by.

43
00:02:08.817 --> 00:02:10.561
This pen belongs to Ana.

44
00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.826
Your turn. Say: Belongs to.

45
00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:17.888
Belongs to.

46
00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.409
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:26.053
Visal, I found a pen. Whose pen is it?

48
00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:37.920
It is Tom's pen. We use 's after a name to show ownership: Tom's pen, the teacher's book, my sister's bag. Whose asks about the owner.

49
00:02:39.017 --> 00:02:40.621
What about plural owners?

50
00:02:41.717 --> 00:02:54.484
If the noun already ends in s, we add only an apostrophe: the students' books. For irregular plurals we add 's: the children's toys. Be careful with the apostrophe.

51
00:02:55.583 --> 00:02:57.235
How do we answer without the noun?

52
00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:10.830
We use mine, yours, his, hers, ours, theirs: Whose bag is this? It's mine. This pen belongs to me. They replace possessive word plus noun.

53
00:03:11.967 --> 00:03:13.328
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.183 --> 00:03:17.692
Grammar focus: Whose and possessive 's and mine, yours.

55
00:03:17.992 --> 00:03:19.167
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.883 --> 00:03:21.627
Tom's pen is on the desk.

57
00:03:22.517 --> 00:03:24.052
Whose bag is this?

58
00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.100
The bag is mine (it belongs to me).

59
00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:38.767
Add 's to a singular owner: Tom's pen. Add only an apostrophe to plural nouns ending in s: the students' books. Whose asks about the owner; mine and yours answer.

60
00:03:39.517 --> 00:03:43.272
Be careful! Don't say: The students book is here.

61
00:03:45.233 --> 00:03:47.929
Say: The students' book is here.

62
00:03:48.229 --> 00:03:50.601
Add an apostrophe for plural owners.

63
00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.018
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:54.833 --> 00:03:55.834
Whose Is It?.

65
00:03:56.134 --> 00:03:58.462
Whose bag is this? It is mine.

66
00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:02.209
This is Tom's book, and that is the girl's pencil.

67
00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.118
The teacher's desk is near the board.

68
00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:08.121
The students' books are on the shelf.

69
00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:12.015
Everything has an owner, and we must respect it.

70
00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:17.404
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:20.322
This is blank pen. (Ana)

72
00:04:20.622 --> 00:04:24.090
A, Ana. B, Ana's. C, Anas.

73
00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:29.366
The answer is B: Ana's.

74
00:04:30.517 --> 00:04:31.866
blank bag is this?

75
00:04:32.166 --> 00:04:36.272
A, Who. B, Whose. C, Who's.

76
00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:41.856
The answer is B: Whose.

77
00:04:43.017 --> 00:04:45.541
The pen belongs to me. It is blank.

78
00:04:45.841 --> 00:04:48.682
A, my. B, mine. C, I.

79
00:04:52.233 --> 00:04:53.943
The answer is B: mine.

80
00:04:55.083 --> 00:04:56.827
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:57.127 --> 00:05:03.428
A, The students books are here.. B, The students' books are here.. C, The student's' books are here..

82
00:05:06.967 --> 00:05:10.290
The answer is B: The students' books are here..

83
00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:14.216
According to the reading, whose desk is near the board?

84
00:05:14.516 --> 00:05:18.436
A, the teacher's. B, Tom's. C, the girl's.

85
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.267
The answer is A: the teacher's.

86
00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:28.374
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:29.217 --> 00:05:32.450
Whose pen is on your desk? Answer with 's or mine.

88
00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.878
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:43.178 --> 00:05:53.510
The pen on my desk is mine. The notebook next to it is Sophea's. I use 's to show that the notebook belongs to my friend Sophea. I use mine when the owner is me.

90
00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:55.449
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:56.350 --> 00:06:01.522
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and whose and possessive 's and mine, yours.

92
00:06:01.822 --> 00:06:05.275
Today's value is respect. Thank the people who help us.

93
00:06:05.575 --> 00:06:08.436
See you in Unit thirty-eight. Goodbye!

94
00:06:08.736 --> 00:06:11.400
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

